--- rendered ---
error[E-unit]: expected `Ω` (a resistance), found `F` (a capacitance)
  --> units.spl:4:44
  |
4 |     let r1 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 10nF };
  |                                            ^^^^ this is `F` (a capacitance)

error[E-unit]: expected `Ω` (a resistance), found `K` (a temperature)
  --> units.spl:5:44
  |
5 |     let r2 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 47K };
  |                                            ^^^ this is `K` (a temperature)
  |
  = help: `K` is kelvin; kilo is lowercase `k`

error[E-unit]: can't add `V` (a voltage) and `A` (a current)
  --> units.spl:6:44
  |
6 |     let r3 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 1V + 1A };
  |                                            ^^^^^^^ different units

error[E-unit]: can't add `Ω` (a resistance) and a plain number
  --> units.spl:7:44
  |
7 |     let r7 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 1V / 1mA + 5 };
  |                                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^ different units

error[E-unit]: temperatures can't be used in arithmetic here
  --> units.spl:8:44
  |
8 |     let r4 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 10°C * 2 };
  |                                            ^^^^^^^^ not a plain quantity

error[E-value]: expected a number
  --> units.spl:9:44
  |
9 |     let r5 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: p };
  |                                            ^ not a number

error[E-value]: `rating` takes an exact value
   --> units.spl:10:57
   |
10 |     let c1 = Capacitor { a: p, b: n, value: 1u, rating: 25V ± 1% };
   |                                                         ^^^^^^^^ a tolerance or range

error[E-value]: a tolerance or range can only be scaled
   --> units.spl:11:45
   |
11 |     let r6 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: (1k ± 1%) + 1k };
   |                                             ^^^^^^^ compute the nominal first, then add the spread
   |
   = note: `2 * (1k ± 1%)` works; adding to a spread doesn't

error[E-value]: range bounds are the wrong way round
   --> units.spl:12:44
   |
12 |     let q1 = Npn { c: p, b: n, e: n, beta: 300..=100 };
   |                                            ^^^^^^^^^ the lower bound comes first
